Based on the analysis of the error log and source code, the segmentation fault in `test_check_flash` is caused by a double-close of a flash area.

The `flash_img_buffered_write()` function, when called with the `flush` parameter set to `true`, writes any remaining buffered data and then closes the flash area associated with the `flash_img_context`.

In `test_check_flash`, `flash_img_buffered_write()` is called with `flush=true`:
```c
ret = flash_img_buffered_write(&ctx, tst_vec, sizeof(tst_vec), true);
```
This closes `ctx.flash_area`. However, at the end of the test function, there is another call to `flash_area_close()`:
```c
flash_area_close(ctx.flash_area);
```
This attempts to close an already closed flash area. With the `CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER` Kconfig option enabled, this double-close leads to an infinite recursion between `flash_area_close` and `boot_close`, causing a stack overflow and a segmentation fault.

The fix is to remove the redundant `flash_area_close(ctx.flash_area)` call at the end of the `test_check_flash` function, as the flash area has already been properly closed by `flash_img_buffered_write()`.

